## ---------------------------------------------------------------
## Spherical inclusion embedded in a unit-cube matrix, domain [0,1]^3
## ---------------------------------------------------------------
reset
undo group begin

## ---- Parameters -----------------------------------------------
#{L     = 1.0}          ## cube edge -> domain [0,L]^3
#{RAD   = 0.25}         ## inclusion radius
#{ESIZE = 0.025}          ## target element size
#{HALF  = L/2}
#{TOL   = L/1.0e4}      ## geometric picking tolerance

## ---- Geometry (built centered on origin, shifted at the end) ----
sphere radius {RAD}                  ## the inclusion, kept
brick x {L}                          ## the matrix
sphere radius {RAD}                  ## sacrificial cutting tool

## Hollow out the matrix. Boolean result may take a new id,
## so compress to force inclusion -> 1, matrix -> 2.
subtract volume 3 from volume 2
compress ids
list volume                          ## expect exactly 2 volumes

## Temporary block membership so scheme assignment survives webcuts.
block 1 volume 1
block 2 volume 2

## Partition into octants for meshability.
## Planes pass through the origin, which is still the sphere center.
webcut volume all with plane xplane
webcut volume all with plane yplane
webcut volume all with plane zplane

## Shift so the matrix occupies [0,L]^3 (mesh not built yet, nothing merged yet)
move volume all x {HALF} y {HALF} z {HALF}

## Enforce a contiguous mesh across the inclusion/matrix interface
imprint volume all
merge all

## ---- Sidesets, picked geometrically on the shifted geometry -----
sideset 1 surface with x_coord < {TOL}
sideset 1 name "left"
sideset 2 surface with x_coord > {L-TOL}
sideset 2 name "right"
sideset 3 surface with y_coord < {TOL}
sideset 3 name "front"
sideset 4 surface with y_coord > {L-TOL}
sideset 4 name "back"
sideset 5 surface with z_coord < {TOL}
sideset 5 name "bottom"
sideset 6 surface with z_coord > {L-TOL}
sideset 6 name "top"

## ---- Meshing ----------------------------------------------------
volume in block 1 scheme tetprimitive
volume in block 2 scheme polyhedron
volume all size {ESIZE}
mesh volume all

## Collapse to one exported element block for thermal input convention.
delete block 1
delete block 2
block 1 hex all
block 1 name "eblock-0_0_0"
undo group end

## ---- Sanity checks ----------------------------------------------
list block all
list sideset all
quality volume all
export Genesis "mesh.exo" dimension 3 block 1 overwrite